WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
14 January 2020, CO2 on a turning globe. Breath, and a heartbeat per day.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.500
The densest CO2 glows orange-red, pulsing over China and drifting east. Oboe follows Asia, harp Oceania.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.000
Late January, Africa comes round. Flute for Europe, marimba for Africa.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Early February. Orange-red flickers across Africa south of the Sahara, where fires burn, pulsing with day and night.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Mid February. South America rises on the left, already orange-red.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Around 20 February. A pulsing orange-red mesh covers South America, densest over the Amazon. Vibraphone for North America, cello for South America.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Late February. Storms swirl tan haze over the United States and the North Atlantic.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.200
Early March: the Americas play to the end.
